adjudication.rationale:
In `packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts` the fallback logic for `updateEvent` was changed to:
```ts
const selectedCalendar = externalCalendarId ? externalCalendarId : event.destinationCalendar?.find(
  (cal) => cal.externalId === externalCalendarId
)?.externalId;
```
When `externalCalendarId` is falsy (the ternary else-branch), the `find` predicate compares `cal.externalId === undefined`, which will not match normal calendars and effectively returns `undefined`. This removes the previous behavior of falling back to the event’s destination calendar externalId and can cause updates to target the default/primary calendar (or lack a proper calendarId depending on downstream usage), leaving the original event stale on the actual destination calendar. The same flawed pattern appears in `deleteEvent`/`calendarId` fallback as well. This is a concrete correctness regression visible in the diff.
